WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.387
A pivot becomes much easier if you break it into four decisions.

00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:07.647
First, define the output grain.

00:00:07.647 --> 00:00:12.662
Second, identify which category values should become columns.

00:00:12.662 --> 00:00:19.392
Third, choose the measure. Fourth, choose the aggregate used to fill each cell.

00:00:19.392 --> 00:00:24.782
For the admissions example, one output row might represent one month.

00:00:24.782 --> 00:00:29.750
The categories are diagnoses, and the measure is the number of admissions.
